# UI color (meaning, not decoration)

Act as a senior product designer and Flutter engineer. Use only `AppColors` / `AppGradients` in `lib/constants/app_theme.dart`. Do not add new hex unless no token fits.

| Meaning | Token |
|---------|--------|
| Delete, remove, reject, error snackbar | `AppColors.danger` |
| Safe action in a destructive dialog (Keep / Stay) | Filled `primaryDark`; destructive is **outline** danger, equal 48px height |
| Approve, saved, done | `AppColors.success` |
| Pending, warning, future | `AppColors.warning` / `pending` |
| Primary proceed (save, apply, clock in) | `AppColors.primaryDark` |
| Admin chrome | `AppGradients.adminBrandHeader` |
| Employee chrome | `AppGradients.brandHeader` / `employeeHeroHeader` |
| Auth / login | `AppGradients.authBackground`, `authNavy` / `authBlue` |
| Clock / wordmark | `teal` / `tealBright` / `AppGradients.tealBadge` |
| Text | `textPrimary` / `textSecondary` / `textHint` |
| Surfaces | `surface`, `cardBg`, `divider`, `cardShadowFaint` |

Confirms: reuse `showAppConfirmDialog` / `AppDialogActions`. Do not use `AlertDialog` actions that stack on a phone.

Status color once (chip or one button). No extra magenta/pink/teal stripes. Unread badges use `danger`, not `Colors.red`.
